# Trust Platform update — sidecar-based Platform-SSO for @@APP_NAME@@

GENERATED by `marketplace/tools/prepare-app`. This records what the tool added to make **@@APP_NAME@@**
deployable in the SAP AI Trust Platform Marketplace with Platform SSO — **without changing the app's
own code**. A Platform-SSO *sidecar* runs in front of the unmodified app.

- **Branch:** `@@BRANCH@@` (baseline: your default branch)
- **App code changed:** none. The app is wrapped, not modified.
- **Deployable image:** `ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:sso` — built from `Dockerfile.platform-sso` and published to
  GitHub Container Registry by `.github/workflows/publish-image.yml` on push to `@@BRANCH@@`.
- **To deploy it in the platform UI:** see [`ui_deploy_guide.md`](./ui_deploy_guide.md).

## How it works

```
browser ─(platform proxy, strips /api/marketplace/v1/proxy/@@SLUG@@ prefix)→ CONTAINER
   sidecar :@@LISTEN_PORT@@  ──(OIDC login, session, then reverse-proxy)──►  @@APP_NAME@@ :@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@ (unchanged)
```

The sidecar terminates the platform login (OIDC Authorization-Code + PKCE against the platform
Keycloak), establishes a session, and forwards every authenticated request to the original app on an
internal port. The app needs no OIDC awareness.

## What the tool added (no existing file was modified)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.platform-sso/sidecar/server.js` + `package.json` | the reusable Platform-SSO OIDC RP reverse proxy |
| `.platform-sso/entrypoint.sh` | starts the app on `:@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@` + the sidecar on `:@@LISTEN_PORT@@` |
| `Dockerfile.platform-sso` | wrapper image = your app image + Node + the sidecar |
| `.github/workflows/publish-image.yml` | builds + publishes `ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:sso` on push |
| `trust_platform_update.md`, `ui_deploy_guide.md` | this doc + the UI deploy checklist |

Your original `Dockerfile`, source, and start command are untouched — the wrapper builds your image as
a base and layers the sidecar on top; the entrypoint runs your original command (bound to
`PORT=@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@`) plus the sidecar.

## Ports

- **App port** to register in the Marketplace = **@@LISTEN_PORT@@** (the sidecar's port).
- The app itself runs internally on **@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@** (never exposed directly).

## Notes / limits

- The sidecar does not rewrite URLs inside HTML/JS bodies. If the app hardcodes root-absolute asset
  paths that don't resolve under the proxy, set `PUBLIC_PATHS` (see `.platform-sso/sidecar/README.md`)
  or give the app a base-href. Redirect `Location` headers are handled by the platform proxy.
- If **@@APP_NAME@@** has its **own** login, users see the platform login (sidecar) first, then the
  app's login. Apps with no own login get a single clean platform login.

Full background: the platform guide `marketplace/docs/onboard-an-app.md`.
